    {
      "text": "Agree with thine adversary quickly, Matt. 5:25 (3 Ne. 12:25). they had disputed among themselves, Mark 9:34. there arose certain … disputing with Stephen, Acts 6:9. he … disputed against the Grecians, Acts 9:29. Paul and Barnabas had no small dissension and disputation with them, Acts 15:2. when there had been much disputing, Peter rose, Acts 15:7. disputed he in the synagogue with the Jews, Acts 17:17. spake … three months, disputing and persuading, Acts 19:8. they neither found me in the temple disputing, Acts 24:12. weak in the faith receive ye, but not to doubtful disputations, Rom. 14:1. where is the disputer of this world, 1 Cor. 1:20. Do all things without murmurings and disputings, Philip. 2:14. Perverse disputings of men of corrupt minds, 1 Tim. 6:5. he disputed about the body of Moses, Jude 1:9.",
